1
00:00:00,958 --> 00:00:09,168
One number unlocks a stranger's secrets.
A login proves only who you are —
never which record truly belongs to you.

2
00:00:10,624 --> 00:00:19,902
Change one digit in the request,
and the same door opens on someone else's life —
handed over unasked.

3
00:00:20,998 --> 00:00:29,928
Firewalls hunt for bad code; this request carries none —
just a valid key tried on the wrong lock,
across a thousand companies.

4
00:00:30,958 --> 00:00:40,368
One missing question fixes this — not who you are,
but whether you own it, ask every time
and the wrong door stays shut.

